  "rationale": "Thinking stays off because with it on the model spent all 300 tokens in reasoning_content and never emitted an answer, which is useless for small coding tasks. MTP is the dominant lever: turning it off halves decode (53.77 -> 25.98 tps) at identical TTFT, and it was already on at baseline, so the sweep's job was to quantify it and then tune its depth. Depth 6 beat the adaptive default by 7% decode and 6% total wall time and was the only depth to rank at the top in both the forward and backward sweep passes, so it is kept. DFlash is mutually exclusive with MTP and, tested with MTP off as required, delivered only +1.6% decode inside noise while being 2.2x slower than MTP overall, so it is rejected. KV quantization is a real win (off is worst in both sweep directions); 4-bit with skip_last is kept over 2-bit because 2-bit's apparent lead was inside noise and 2-bit KV is a genuine quality risk on code, and skip_last keeps the most recent tokens at full precision, which is what matters for code. Context 32768 beat native 262144 by 3.5% TTFT and 4% decode in a paired interleaved A/B, so it is kept. Sampling is set to coding defaults with force_sampling so the profile's sampler is authoritative. All three quality-guardrail prompts pass at this configuration.",
